</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 482)</h2>
<p><b>The playlist shows which shots have optimized media.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>New: a bolt beside each shot that has a stand-in ready</b>, and a count in the playlist header — "⚡ 8" against 13 shots is the answer to "is this session ready to send?" without opening anything. Only optimized shots are marked; a column of thirteen badges would be noise.</li>
<li>The marks track what is actually on disk: they appear as each shot finishes rendering, and clear when you delete stand-ins or switch optimized media off.</li>
<li><b>A shot whose render has been updated since its stand-in was made shows as not optimized</b>, which is the honest answer — playback ignores a stale stand-in too, so marking it ready would be a lie.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
